ompetency, Good Judgment, Self-control (26 TAC §746.1201(1))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1091885-i20250623-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1091885-i20250623","date":"2025-06-23","original_code":"746.1205(a)(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-09-17","finding":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity: A child in care sustained a serious injury and the caregiver was not aware of how the injury occurred.  The child was not participating in class and could not bear weight on the leg.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026680694","violation_type_title":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1091885-i20250623-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-307-b-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1091885-i20250623","date":"2025-06-23","original_code":"746.307(b)(1)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-09-17","finding":"AP Parental Communication - Injury Requires Treatment by Health Care Professional or Hospitalization: A child sustained a broken femur.  The caregiver was unaware of the injury.  Medical stated this type of injury is immediately noticeable and the child would cry.  The child did cry and the staff saw similar signs of the child's constipation. However, the child could not bear weight which not a symptom of his constipation.  The parent was not informed of this other symptom.  The child was crying from the end of nap to pick up at 5:55pm.","topic":"health","source_record_id":"1026690814","violation_type_title":"AP Parental Communication -